  "limits": [
    "The DTM interpolates moat-height ground across the keep court and lower heights into some building footprints. The raised keep court and bounded foundations are reconstructed using open main-court controls, not a claim of surveyed floor levels.",
    "Older BD TOPO base/roof altitude fields disagree with this working DTM by up to several meters. Published relative keep height is retained; incompatible absolute roof fields do not control placement. Acquisition date and exact current entrance/bridge grades remain unverified.",
    "One-meter source and two-meter diagnostic sampling are not survey accuracy. Bounded foundations fill only architecture and the reconstructed inner court. No full-site slab or terrain cutout.",
    "Bridge slopes and masonry batters are bounded exterior reconstructions; no walkable interiors or exact present-day structural survey."
  ],
  "inspection": {
    "reviewedOn": "2026-10-11",
    "frames": 55,
    "notes": "All55 final normal-placement image pixels actually inspected: master/four tiers at whole compound, keep/chatelet, chapel west, royal court, Village gate, plan, keep west moat, Bois gate and three bridge side views. Each state samples signed anchor once; three outside-ground probes agree with rendered triangles within0.0151m fixture offset, three outward foundation contacts and four gate voids pass per state. Raised inner court is bounded and roofless. Corrected winding closes exterior arch spandrels and sloped deck/support gaps in the inspected side views. Coarse retained terrain still rises inside under-arches; no navigable underpass or exact moat-bottom claim. Bounded foundations remain buried; surrounding host ground is unchanged. Five unloads release geometry and preserve ground. Current surveyed levels and acquisition date are unknown."
  }
